course: dictionary
lesson: 14422
title: Going past the mark
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Overshot is the past form of overshoot. It means you went past the place, line or target you were aiming for. «The bus driver overshot the stop, so we had to walk back.» The bus went beyond the stop. Nobody meant it to, but it happened.
explain: Overshot can also be about amounts. «We overshot the budget and had less money for the trip.» You spent more than the plan allowed. The past form is overshot, so write overshot, not overshooted.
explain: Check the meaning by swapping in went past. «The ball overshot the goal» means the ball went past the goal. If the sentence still makes sense, you have found the right meaning.
fact: Overshoot is the base verb, and overshot is its past form: overshoot, overshoots, overshot, overshooting.
fact: «Overshot» means went past a place, line or target by mistake.
fact: «Overshot» can also mean went over a planned amount, time or budget.
fact: An overshot water wheel is turned by water poured onto its top.
fact: In maths, overshooting means going past the target number, and then you correct back.
exercise: «The car overshot the turning and had to reverse.» What does overshot mean here? | Stopped exactly on time | Turned left quickly | Waited patiently | *Went past by mistake
exercise: «We overshot our budget for the party.» What does overshot mean? | Counted the coins carefully | Saved money for later | *Spent more than planned | Spent nothing at all
exercise: «Yesterday the footballer overshot the goal by a metre.» Find and copy the word that is the past form of overshoot. | footballer | metre | goal | *overshot
test: «The mill had an overshot wheel, turned by water poured onto its top.» What is an overshot wheel? | A bicycle wheel | *A water wheel turned by water falling onto its top | A spinning top for children | A wheel on a toy car
test: Ben says overshot means stayed exactly where he was. Is he right? | No, it means went to sleep | Yes, it means stayed still | *No, overshot means went past the target | Yes, it means stopped early
exam: The recipe said add 2 cups, but Sam overshot and added 3. What does overshot mean in this story? | Read the recipe twice | *Added more than the amount planned | Added less than the amount planned | Did not add anything at all
